given-names></name><name><surname>Schulz</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name></person-group></citation></ref><ref id="r17"><citation citation-type="journal"><article-title>Deregulation of c-myc gene expression in human colon carcinoma is not accompanied by amplification or rearrangement of the gene.</article-title><source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source><volume>5</volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>1969</fpage><lpage>1976</lpage><year>1985</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3837853</pub-id><person-group><name><surname>Erisman</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Rothberg</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Diehl</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Morse</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Spandorfer</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Astrin</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group></citation></ref><ref id="r18"><citation citation-type="journal"><article-title>Control of c-myc regulation in normal and neoplastic cells.</article-title><source>Adv. Cancer Res.</source><volume>51</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><year>1991</year><person-group><name><surname>Spencer</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Groudine</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2028839</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r19"><citation citation-type="journal"><article-title>TFIIH operates through an expanded proximal promoter to fine-tune c-myc expression.</article-title><source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source><volume>25</volume><fpage>147</fpage><lpage>161</lpage><year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15601838</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/MCB.25.1.147-161.2005</pub-id><person-group><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><s